<LLMTokenQuota name="LTQ-User-Enforce" continueOnError="false" enabled="true">
  <DisplayName>LLM Token Quota Tier 3 -- one user within their department within this use case (enforce)</DisplayName>
  <Operation>EnforceOnly</Operation>
  <!--
    Added 2026-09-17. Innermost tier. Identified by llm_dept_app_user
    (department:client_id:oid, built by AM-Identity.xml).

    Cannot reuse UseQuotaConfigInAPIProduct here — that mechanism reads the
    product's ONE llmQuota field, already spent on Tier 1's full-ceiling-per-
    app design (LTQ-App-Enforce.xml). A genuinely narrower Tier-3 number
    needs its own value, so this reads a product attribute directly instead,
    the same Allow/countRef shape every plain Quota policy in this codebase
    already uses (Q-PerAppDay.xml, Q-PerUser.xml on mcp-v1, etc.).

    UNVERIFIED AGAINST A LIVE DEPLOY: this is the first LLMTokenQuota policy
    in this codebase NOT using UseQuotaConfigInAPIProduct. The plain Quota
    policy schema supports Allow/Interval/TimeUnit as an alternative to
    reading the product config, and LLMTokenQuota is documented as an
    extension of that schema, but nothing here has actually exercised this
    path yet. Confirm with a debug session on first deploy that this element
    combination is accepted and that the count/countRef pair resolves the way
    every other Quota policy's does — do not assume it from this comment
    alone.
  -->
  <Allow count="2000000" countRef="verifyapikey.VA-ApiKey.apiproduct.llm_tokens_per_hour_user"/>
  <Interval>1</Interval>
  <TimeUnit>hour</TimeUnit>
  <Identifier ref="llm_dept_app_user"/>
  <LLMModelSource>{llm.model}</LLMModelSource>
  <LLMTokenUsageSource>0</LLMTokenUsageSource>
</LLMTokenQuota>
